    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d45">

                <pb facs="0062" n="50" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg50"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">123 EN 3/710: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Iran</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Dreyfus</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tehran</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-04-22T10:00:00+03:25">April 22, 1942—10
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received noon.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>116. Afghan Minister informs me his Government has now given formal consent to
                    appointment of Engert as Envoy Extraordinary and Minister Plenipotentiary of the
                    United States at Kabul. I have asked him to ascertain in view of this
                    development whether his Government will now grant permission for Thayer to
                    proceed to Kabul to open the Legation.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dreyfus</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
